        <p>FRIDAY, OCTOBER 23, 1896</p>
        <p>FURNISH AT WORSLEY'S,</p>
        <p>"THE PANTHEON." GAYTHORN, MANCHESTER.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-24_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>BY POST 1. 70 per,Quarter, 6s.6d.per Annum 1..9d per Quarter credit</head>
        <p>BY POST 1. 70 per,Quarter, 6s.6d.per Annum 1..9d per Quarter credit</p>
        <p>HIGH-CLASS SECOND-HAND FURNITURE, FURNITURE BY JAMES LAMB. GOODALL, GANNETT, GILLOWS, STARKEY AND MELD, HENRY OGDEN AND SONS, DOViiSTON, DYSON, MAPLE, AND</p>
        <p>SCHOOLBRED. CRUSHING DEFEAT OF HIGH PRICES.</p>
        <p>UT EEKLY CHA T.—We respectfully draw attention this week to the various lots we are specially advertising. The terms of purchase will include delivery, and a guarantee for each lot for five years. The list we give beow forms only a small and infinitesimal part of th,- bargains we have on view at The Pantheon." What we are advertising to-day is an illustration of what we can do, and what we have on show. Inspection invited.</p>
        <p>(19MPLETE HOUSES OF FURNITURE. k.) Lot 1. Splendid House of Furniture, containing Din- ing-room, Drawing-room, Sitting-room. Kitchen, and four Bedrooms. Cost £2lO. Our price. £B5. Lot 2 . Excellent House of Furniture for a Working-man for £2O, consisting of a solid ahogany Dining-room Suite, Dining-table. Sideboard, Carpet, Brass Fender and Brasses, Kitchen Chairs, Table, Oilcloth, ling, Fender. Ashpan. Fire- iro,is •' Bedroom Suite, Brass and Enamelled Bedstead. Mat- tress. Bed. Bolster and Pillows, Carpet, Toilet Ware. and side sundries. A Wonderful bargain. Lot 3. An Exceptional Offer. We can offer a splendid Bargain in a House of Furniture for £4O. The Furniture is all well-made. very stylish, and equal to new. The Dining- roma' is furnished in Solid Oak and Morocco. The Sitting- roord in Solid Mahogany. There is also Kitchen Furniture and two Bedrooms very handsomely furnished. A complete list will be sent on application, post free. We have on view completl Houses of Furuiture from £lO up to £5OO. Full and complete list of each will be sent post free, on application.</p>
        <p>DINING-ROOM FURNITURE. Lot 50. Seen-Id-hard Sminish Mahogany Dining-room Suite. in Morocco, handsomely carved for R.S.</p>
        <p>Lot; 51 :econd-hand Am e;ican Wa nut Dining-room Suite in leather. £4 15s.</p>
        <p>Lot 52: Second-hand Brown Oak Dining-room Suite, in velvet, 5 guineas Lot 53. An extraordinary Massive Dining-room Suite, in Spanish Mahogany, consisting of a spoon-back Suite, of Couch, ,wo Easy Chairs, and six Single Chairs, upholstered In Morocco, Magnificent Spanish Mahogany Sideboard to match, with lofty plate-glass back. most beautifully carved in good preservation. 10ft. Di, ins-table on massive carved sup- ports. !his lot is worth to-day £lOO. and cost over £2OO when new, and will be sold a bargain tor £4O. Lot 54. Fine old Spanish Sideboard, 7ft. 6in, long, in Spanish mahogany, cost £7O. Lot 56. Second hand Dining-room Suite complete, with Sideboard, Tabie. and Overmatitel, the suite upholstered in Moroceo. Cost £B6 Price guineas. Lot 57 Good Second-hand Dining-room Suite, of nine pieces, splendid Sideboard and Dining Table to seat 10 per- sons, together with the Overmantel. Ourprice for quick sale 15 guineas. Lot 58. Magnificent Pollard Oak Dining-room Seite, suit- able for a nobleman. This Furniture is second-hand, but it I, quite equal to new, having been entirely re-upholstered in Morocco ; it is in beautifulcondition,and spotless throughout. The design is original, and is by a celebrated maker. The Sideboard is 7ft long, palatial in size, and beautiful in de- sign ; the wood is the very finest figured Pollard Oak. The earring is executed in fine has relief,and is a work of art. The Suite is by Taylor and Whitfield; the carving alone must have cost a fabulous sum. Consists of very beautiful Coach. pair of Easy Chairs, and six Single Chairs. We can Provi le 12 Single Chairs if necessary. The Dining Table is 18ft lon and matches the rest of the Furniture. We have not the slightest hesitation in declaring that this Furniture Is worth £5OO. Our price for the lot is £2OO. N.B.—lt will be seen by the let 58 we have just described that V?ORSLISY'S must have a very extensive stock. We have just described three pieces of Furniture for £2OO, and while In Lot 57 we give a lot for Diningroom for 15 gui:-seas. show- ing what a wide and Extensive Stock Worsley's have on show. We have over 100 complete Diningroom Suites on show, besides scores of odd Sideboards and odd Dining Tables.</p>
        <p>DRAWING-ROOM FURNITURE. In this Department we have perhaps the finest selec- tion of Furniture to be seen in any house in the country. It is very difficult to select out of the bargains on view in this room a few that will convey a fair idea of their ma tnifi- cence and quality in this short paragraph; there are such a quantity of them. We have over Y.OO Drawing-room Suites on show in every variety of colour and shade of upholstery. We give one or two examples : Lot 215. Very exquisitely pretty and unique Chippendale Drawing-room Suite for £l2. perhaps the greatest marvel of any bargain that has been offered; it is quite sufficient to say that tWe Suite is beautifully inlaid and covered in the finest silk tapestry. It is a second-hand suite which has been re covered and re polished, and entirely renovated, and is now entirely equal to new. It would undoubtedly compare favourably with anything that is being offered for £25 and £3O eleewhere. We have the Cabinet to match at the same price, £l2. This is just as beautifully made, contains numerous shelves for bric-a-brac, and splendidly fitted with bevel plates; there is also an overmantel, which matches. for 3 guineas. two Occasional Tables at 18s, each. a Music Cabinet for £2 155., and Lady's Writing Table for £3 10s. ; altosether forming the prettiest collection ot Chippendale furnitnre which leas ever been on show at the price. Lots 310 to 330. A Fine Collection of 20 Second-hand Cabi- nets and Chiffoniers, from £2 108. up to £lO. These have been marked exceedingly low.to clear, and are of the good old-fashioned make. Everyone of these are second-hand.</p>
        <p>Lots 351 to 365 - Fourteen Wonderfully Cheap Overtnintels, second-hand. Some of these cost as much as £2O. We shill offer them from 30s. to £5.</p>
        <p>Lot 366. SPECIAL BARGAIN, The Prettiest. Best, and Cheapest Drawing-room Suite ever offered. This Suite is of exceptional merit ; it consists of the sweetest designed Settee, and pair of Easy Chairs, two exquisite Occasional uhairs,and two beautiful Single Chairs. The whole is very prettily in- laid w th ivory, and upholstered in silk tapestry ; well worth 255. per yard. 't he Cabinet to match is of a design both weird and pe dfliar ;curious littla columns with nithes ior the display of china,grotesque little cupboards fitted with bevelled crystals, special cover, and of peculiar shape for five o'clock tea service; two of the trickiest little tables imaginable, a peculiar and beautiful little Overmantel to match the lot, design of which is just as grotesque and curious as the rest of Furniture. This is the kind of Suite that lad es tall in love with wherever it is seen. Our price for the lot 21t guineas, BEDROOM FURNITURE. w 0 RSLEY'S have the Biggest Show of Bedroom Furni- ture of anyone in the United Kingdom. We are quite aware that most Houses lay maim to having the Biggest Stock, but we challenge any intending purchaser to compare by inspec- tion the Knormous Stock of Bedroom Furniture at WORS- LKY'S with that of any other House in the Kingdom We have over 300 Bedroom Suites on show. We have just com- pleted another contract for 300 B:clioom Suites for our stock, and we have in process of manutacture,orders with manufac- turers of bedsteads which shall bring our stock to little short of 1,030 edsteada. Out of this varied collection we select a few sample bargains only. SPECIAL NOTION. 'You might hear a remark that it is very seldom ton visit WORsLEY'S but that you can pick up such a bargain that more than repays the trouble of your visit. ' Lot 789. A Magnificent Pollard 'Yak BEDROOM SUITR will be sold a bargain tos £l2O which siriginally coat £5OO. This is the finest bedeoom suite in Manchester. Lot 792. A Very Handsome Bedroom Suite, smaller in sin, suitable for a young lady's bedroom, exquisitely pretty, of a nlassical design, and the beet workmanship throughout ; price 10 guineas. We have a tremendous Stock of Odd Wardrob-s, in all kind of woods. We have Wardrobes, 6ft. long, enamelled woods, eontaming numerous drawers, tray shelves, and hanging compartments ; these run from £2 no to £6 Cs. We have next a big collection of Washstands and Dressing- tables in mahogany, walnut, oak, and enamelled woods. We can do a magnificent Pair of Mahogany Stands for £ S 10s. We have Walnut Stands. the pair complete, for £2 15s and upsa cis. We have Open Stands from 12s 64. But ii you want a bargain, no matter whether you wish to give £5 or £5O. you can meet with what you require at W Otis Y'S. Lot 796. The Dressing '1 able and Washstand to match, sft ; fine, handsome, massive, and richly figuted iii toe wood. This is a very bold and large p.ir of Cheval Stands, price £25. The same could not be o'itaincd for £.O else-</p>
        <p>We crnmot trespass on the spaee of this paper to any greater estent We shall issuers new advertisement, with anew list next week. Don't forget that we are quite willing to show you all our bargains, whether ou buy co, not, and that it you do purchase and do not require immediate delivery we will In ore them free of charge. MN* aisama • BEDSTii‘ ADS and BEDDING. Lot 1,101. Magnificent becond-hind Solid Brass I:ldsteads, beautifully chased, splendid design; cost £2O. for 23 10s Lot 1.105 Very handsome Solid Brass Persian Bed,tead massive pillars ; cost £3O, lor 10 guineas. Lot 1,107. Job lot of Secone-hand Persian Bedsteads to be sold cheap. from 15s to 30s.</p>
        <p>Lot 1,141. Fifty Second-hand Fr. ruth Eltdtteads to be cleared out at any price. from 43 6d to lOs 6d. Lot 1,192. A *Job lot, all olid Brass Bedstends, slightly soiled, from 25. to £3 10s.</p>
        <p>'ERAS t= FKNDERS and BRAS.? FS, Lot 1,786. Magnificent Suite of Sold Brass Fender, Pair of magniacent flogs, end Patent stop : all sPcond-hand; equal to new; Post E 2.5 ; or £3 10s. Lot 1,789. Very handsome second-hand Brass Curb, Dogs, and Brasses ; cost £lO for 35s • _ .</p>
        <p>Lot 1,790.. Elegant Nevi- Fire Suite, consisting of benutiful chaPed fender, pair of very handsome dogs. and set of exquis ite fire brasses, all quite new designs. 'llie suite conililete for 2 guineas. Lot 1,791 Very good So,;(1 Bass and Rname'led Suite of Fender, Brasses, and Dogs, for Gls ;honestly worth £4. Lot 1,792. Very Heavy olid 13ress Fender, second-hand. cost ES ;3 .a</p>
        <p>Lot 1,793. New Solid Brass Fire Suite,consisting of feeder, bratses, and dogs: splendid design, for 19s 6d Lot 1,794. Job Lot of Soiled Fenders, from 4s 6d to half - *-guinea. Some ot these finders are worth several pounds'.</p>
        <p>W. H. AV ORsLE Y, " THE PANTHEON,' ir- GAYTHOHN, 31 ANCHESTEII, All City-mad Cars Pass Business Hcurs, WORolaßl'd. • 9to 7.</p>
