      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-24_WidnesExaminer_art0012" n="art0012">
        <head>PUREST OF WATERS.</head>
        <p>THE PUREST OF WATERS.</p>
        <p>INVALUABLE TO INVALIDS.</p>
        <p>It greatly improves the avour of 'Wines, Spirits etc..</p>
        <p>Ask for it e. your Chemists or Hotel.</p>
        <p>Wholesale only from</p>
        <p>S. GROUNDS,</p>
        <p>WESTON POINT, RUNCORN.</p>
        <p>DUNVILLICS OLD IRI3H WHISKY -</p>
        <p>Has gained SEVENTEEN MEDALS at various great Inter- national Exhibitions. It is sold by every respectable deAler in the world. Quota- tions on application to the Head 0 ffices, Belfast. x</p>
        <p>IOLD ATININIS T AS A PROFITABLE INVESTMENT. Parties with a little spare Pash at their command would do well to pondsr over the following remarks. It is a well known fact that many worthy families in this and other counties laid the founiation of their fortunes by investing in I.gitimate mining enterprises. What has been dono t-efore can be done again, but investors should make strict and careful enquiries before embirking in undertakings of this description. There can be os doubt that if a judicious selection be made of the various public companies Low work- ing, the shares in wh;ch (owing to th,. great depression) are quoted at merely nominal figures, and an investment made say in half a dozen. we dare sai e y say that in the course of a few months, an investor would see his money doubled or even trebled.</p>
        <p>_ We do not advocate gambling or take prices by the so-called " Cover System," but advise our clients to calculate the num- ber of shares they can takc up and pay tor, to lock them up and watch the price lists. When a profit is shewn, wire or send orders to sell, unless trustworthy advice is received to contraly. Ntto be alarmed at a slight fall in price—in many Instances prices are put down by market manipulation and not because of any falling off n the intrinsic veins of the mine—but wire or inf. rrmation.and if there is any legitimate reason sot the fall, sell out and cut the loss. By followinte the abave faithfully, risks are reduced to a. minimum and large profits can be, made. We may' mention another form of alining investment which has proved wonderfully profitable in the entree of the past few years. we iefer to exploration and development syndi- cates. These syndicates are formes to explore certain gold fields, diseover and open out mines, An% With undertakings of this kinds small amount of capital only is required. Claims can be purchased first hand from prospectors or discovered and acquired by agents ef th. syndicate, and proved and developed to an extent suffi,.ient to warrant the formation or separate companies to work them Now a Syndicate of this desc,ii.tion will frequently acquire si.fficient claims or grant for a dozen companies, the sale of a single group alone paying back the entire capital two or three times over, so that in the event of a successful floata- tion of half a dozen c .mpa iies, the shareholders in the ori- ginal Syndicate would hive their capital returned many times ovn in cash teeides retairring a large it-erect in the various companies form d A Preliminary Syndicate of this description is no r iil C011r“,.. of negociation, not for the pur- pose of discovering gold elaams, hut to acquire a number of claims already found and pmveri, 'The country to which this Nyndicate proposes to carry out its first operations has beets one of the richest gold producers in the world, bin th -re has b- n no rush or exeitement, as Its the days of Californian, Austral tn. Sent h African and Wtstralian discoveries, for the simple reason that it has not been advertised. Prospectors are quietly toiling along, mining and crushing the ore and extractiiig the gold by very crude and ancient methods and tu rlcing goad prcfits, not- withstanding the p un tive procesBes employed. 1 he Projector of tr is Syndicate having been engaged in the miniait industry in the.country for teveral years, is welt acquaint -d with the fleia, and has every confidence that when these mines are taken up and w)rked by modern methods large and priifitable returud must be made. Further particulars can be obtained of N ANDREWS et JOMPANY, MINING AGENTS AND SHAREHOLDERS, 105, LONDON WALL. LONDON, B.C. 20 Years' Experience in lingland,'Africa, and South America. Mining Shares bought and reit at close Market Prices. Corresponde On invited. , Te'.egraohie Address •• Orict,ra, LoaDON." Bankers :- BROWN, J•NREN &amp; CO.</p>
