      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-24_WidnesExaminer_art0014" n="art0014">
        <p>BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>AIuNICIPAL ELECTION, NOVEMBER 2ND.1896. TO TICS ICLICCTORi OF ST. AUSTIN'S WAtiD. LADIES AND GENTLEMEN.-</p>
        <p>A large number of influential and ;ndependent ratepayers of this Ward having called upon me and solicited me to :be a 'Candidate for Municipal honours, I have, after due considerstion. allowed myself to be nominated for the position of one ,of your Kepresenratives in the Town Council for this Ward. I am. and have been interested in and also the manager of the firne.of Me,ors. Monks, Hall &amp; Co., Limited, for more than twenty years, and as a very old resident in the Word, / am well acquainted with its requirements. There ere many m.sterial questions affecting the interests of the Ward, which require immediate attention. There is the improvement o Bridge Street, and I think the sooner this is effected the better it will be for the town. lam certainly in 'avcarr ot Progrescion, at the same time I think thereis room to lower the rates, consistent with the well-being of the Borough and if you do me the honour to elect me, I arc resolved to look thoroughly into this question. , The less the rates, the more manufactories we shall have in our Town, a largar amount of employment, and of course greater pr niperity</p>
        <p>The pollution of the river Mersey, and Iso its navigation, will have my earneit attention.</p>
        <p>The making of New Streets also require attention. and I certainly think the period allowed to propetty owners for the payment of street-mllcior„ is too short, and I will vote, if elected, for an extention of time.</p>
        <p>No Pig Market tior Cattle Market, if I can prevent it, shall be allowed to be placed in this Ward. I assure you, Ladies and Gentlemen, that in this Ward your interest Is my interest, and anything that I can do In making the town a good commercial centre, will have my most energetic and closo attention.</p>
        <p>Believe me, Lidies and Gentlemen, Faithfully yours, THOS. BURTON. Tile ',lollies, Liverpool Road, Warrington. 12th October, I£9t3.</p>
        <p>I\7o P43IT of :he world. ',wiring settlers. offers brighter i. prospects to the Agriculturist than</p>
        <p>oNTAiho.</p>
