        <head>EIBITION AT MANCHESTER.</head>
        <p>EIBITION AT MANCHESTER.</p>
        <p>An exhibition which prom6es to have a most mincer ful run for two weeks was opi.tied at St. Jame,'s Manchest.t.r, on MotAlay afternoon. by Mr. T. Fleciclit of Birmingham, the president of the National Associato; of Master Bakers and Confectioners. Mr. J. HailwoOP' president of the Manchester Master Bakers' Associatict presided, and it was stated that this was the first el hibition of its kind that has been held out of LondO, It as complete before it was opened, and never agog', in the history of the trade had there been such r, artistic array of baking and contectionery sent in competition for valuable prizes, tin re being upwartit; 1,600 entries in the two sections, which were arranged thc secretary of The National Association, Mr. A. Last, acting as honorary secretary to the competitil fhe exhibition is under the genera.l management, Mr. Albert P. Baker, who has for many yeers been 07.1 nected with exhibitions in all parts of the world, and:l has successfully produced four previous exhibition Manchester. Most of the principal firms throughS the country have exhibits comprising the latest mact ery and other appliances requisite for the modern b, and oonfecti ner. A. working bakery is in full operatio:i as well as the manufacturing of sweets. The illutninet; fairy fountain is again a c,,rispicin-uts feature of the hibition. The band of the 114al Marine Light Infaos, Portsmouth Division, under the conductor,hip of ip:l George Miller, Moe.. Bac., Cantab., is in attendance week, and the Grenadier Guard's 84n4 will provide music during next week. Li,,ut Dan. Glurrev, Pre; R. A. M., who is retiring from th- army, will 0010 the latter band, with which he has for a great nutli A of years been associated as bandmaster, for the Cl,' time. The management have decided to give tarn benefit on Friday the 30. h inst. The exhibitOn filled on Monday evening by ladies and gentlemen " took a lively interest in the exhibits.</p>
        <p>Lord 11,,sebery opened a TechnicA and Univer4 Extension College and School of Science and Art Jj Colchester on Tuesday and was aft-.rwards the Crj guest at the annul Oyster F-ast, when ho replied to' critics on the Armenian cvi.grinn inv.,l rnwi lansfi4</p>
