        <p>THE CHURCH Roox.—The managers of the above have just received a handsome gift from Mr. John Cros.. field, of Walton Lea. Amongst the various classes, &amp;c., held in the room is a Men's Bible Class every Sunda y afternoon from 2.30 to 3.30, attended by a good number of men in all stations of life. For some time the want of a harmonium for the accompaniment of the hymns &amp;c., has been felt,a want which the managers could no supply. The matter,however, coming to Mr. Crosfield' knowledge was soon settled by his usual prompt aecer- osity and on Wednesday last a fine instrument by Doherty of Ontario (a noted maker of these organs) ar- rived as a present from Mr. Crosfield. It is needless to say how such a kind and thoughtful gift is appreciated, both by the managers of the room and the members of the bible class. Mr. Crosfield has taken a deep interest in the room ever since its inception, in the first instance generously guaranteeing the amount required for its purchase,&amp;c., and on many occasions since, showing his interest in the work carried on in the room, and it is greatly due to him that Buell a room was ever obtained. What would be done in the parish without it is hard to conceive, so useful has it been found in many ways and judging from the arrangements for the coming winter its usefulness seems to be on the increas3.</p>
